{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand your visiting nurse was concerned about your right below-knee amputation site?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, she said there’s a little spot where bone might be showing. But I’m not in pain or anything. I feel fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You were just here two days ago for vomiting, but that’s resolved now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that passed. Just felt flu-like. But this leg—I haven’t had any pain or fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. I examined your right BKA site. There’s a small erosion, about half a centimeter, over the tibia with a bit of bone exposed and mild clear drainage. No redness or pus, which is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a concern because exposed bone can get infected. Your white blood cell count is slightly elevated, which suggests some inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had diabetes for years and these amputations—this kind of thing keeps happening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. With your history, we have to be extra careful. We’ll start IV antibiotics tonight to prevent a deeper infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, but I don’t want to stay long. I just got home yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you overnight for antibiotics and wound care. But I should tell you—the best long-term fix is surgery to cover the exposed bone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Surgery? Again? I’m not ready for that right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I hear you. We won’t push it tonight. But it’s important you come back next week for the procedure, or the infection risk stays high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I go home tomorrow then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if you’re stable. We’ll switch you to oral antibiotics—Bactrim twice a day for 14 days—and manage pain as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my insulin? My sugar was high last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2142-04-22 23:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep your Lantus and Humalog as before. Your glucose was 433 tonight—high, but not critical. We’ll monitor it and adjust if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2142-04-23 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well overnight. No fever, vitals stable. We’re going to discharge you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2142-04-23 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. But I’ll come back for surgery next week, I promise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2142-04-23 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Watch for fever, increased drainage, or redness spreading. Call us if any of that happens."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2142-04-23 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll keep the wound clean and covered?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2142-04-23 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re sending you home with nursing support to help with wound checks and meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2142-04-23 10:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my other medicines—gabapentin, metoprolol?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2142-04-23 10:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All continued. We adjusted gabapentin to 400 mg three times a day. Everything else stays the same, including your heart and mood meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2142-04-23 10:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the morphine? Only if I need it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2142-04-23 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, sustained-release morphine every 8 hours if you need it, plus hydrocodone for breakthrough pain. But use sparingly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2142-04-23 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll follow up and come back for surgery as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2142-04-23 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll see you next week. Take care and call anytime if something changes."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2142-04-22 23:19:00",
    "admission_end": "2142-04-23 12:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 58-year-old woman with type 1 diabetes and bilateral below-knee amputations was admitted after her visiting nurse noted a small erosion with exposed bone on her right amputation site. She denied pain, fever, or systemic symptoms and had been recently discharged two days prior for a brief episode of vomiting. Examination revealed a 0.5 cm area of serous drainage over the tibial tuberosity without erythema or purulence. Laboratory results showed mild leukocytosis and elevated glucose. She was treated with IV antibiotics and wound care. Surgery was recommended to cover the exposed bone, but the patient declined immediate intervention and planned to return the following week. She was discharged home with nursing support, oral Bactrim for 14 days, and instructions to monitor for signs of infection. Follow-up was arranged for surgical evaluation.",
    "problems": [
      "Infection (chronic) of amputation stump",
      "Chronic systolic heart failure",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Amputation of limb(s) causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Old myocardial infarction",
      "Peripheral vascular disease, unspecified",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Pure hyperglyceridemia"
    ]
  }
}
